  "term": "nervous prostration",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, nervous prostration was a popular name for neurasthenia: a state of marked nervous weakness or exhaustion. The source also uses it for chronic exhaustion thought to arise from weakening conditions, as opposed to a more constitutional form.",
